// Title: a bind under an abstract constructor pattern inside an or-pattern
// is never typed: the check accepts any use of it.
// Command: graphix --no-cache c-pattern-or-abstract-payload-untyped.gx
//   (and graphix --check c-pattern-or-abstract-payload-untyped.gx)
// Expected: refused by the check: n is an i64 (T's representation), and
// str::len takes a string.
// Observed: --check accepts it; the run panics:
//   kernel param `n`: runtime I64(3) does not match the compiled String slot
//   Error: runtime did not respond
// (--no-fusion runs str::len over an i64 and prints nothing.) The same with
// `T(n) | S(n)` over [T, S], and `(T(n), 1) | (T(n), 2)` over (T, i64).
// When another alternative binds the name outside a payload, the payload's
// type is left out of the union: in
//   let g = |v: [(string, i64), (T, i64)]| select v {
//     (x, 1) | (T(x), 2) => select x { string as s => s, T as _ => "t" }, _ => "miss" };
//   g((T(4), 2))
// x is typed [string, T] (no i64) and both engines report "select x {..}: no
// arm matches i64:4: a coverage hole in the check".
type T = Abstract<i64>;
let f = |v: [`A(T), `B(T)]| select v { `A(T(n)) | `B(T(n)) => str::len(n) };
f(`A(T(3)))
